// design-system-kit 0.5.2 · profile shadcn · wiring: React Doctor overrides
//
// For repos that run React Doctor (TTT's starter does, on every PR). Setup
// adds these objects to the app's doctor.config.json "ignore.overrides" list
// (creating the file beside package.json if there isn't one, or the
// "reactDoctor" key in package.json if the repo configures it there); it never
// edits the repo's own rules. Paths follow the repo's aliases, as in
// oxlint.design-system.jsonc. Proven on the Districtly run: 35 findings on a
// fresh setup, 3 after, all three the repo's own.
//
// The same reasons as the oxlint override, for the same paths:
// - Vendored stock components are wrappers: roles, handlers, labels and link
//   content arrive through props the scanner can't see, and DatePicker focuses
//   its calendar on open on purpose. shadcn's own markup (a role on <nav>, a
//   role on the breadcrumb's current page, index keys on a static error list)
//   stays as shadcn ships it, so stock files stay comparable to stock.
// - cva variant helpers and DatePicker's documented helpers (patternFor,
//   hintFor, parseTyped) are exported beside the component by design.
// - Kit tests assert on elements they just rendered.
// - Kit scripts are checked in the kit, not per client.
// Every other rule still runs on these files: the scan stays on for anything
// a client changes.
[
  {
    "files": ["src/components/ui/**", "src/hooks/use-mobile.ts"],
    "rules": [
      "react-doctor/only-export-components",
      "react-doctor/prefer-tag-over-role",
      "react-doctor/no-redundant-roles",
      "react-doctor/no-array-index-as-key",
      "react/only-export-components",
      "react/set-state-in-effect",
      "jsx-a11y/prefer-tag-over-role",
      "jsx-a11y/click-events-have-key-events",
      "jsx-a11y/no-noninteractive-element-interactions",
      "jsx-a11y/label-has-associated-control",
      "jsx-a11y/no-autofocus",
      "jsx-a11y/anchor-has-content",
      "typescript/no-non-null-assertion"
    ]
  },
  { "files": ["scripts/**"] }
]
